  "_local_axis": "LOCAL-RUNNABLE is a declared third axis (Ren, 2026-08-19): can a person run this on their own consumer hardware, free, offline, with no data leaving the machine? That is not the cheap end of a price ladder, it is a different category -- no API, no per-call cost, no third party. RAM figures are approximate and assume ~4-bit quantisation.",
  "_free_endpoint_rule": "':free' variants price at $0, which is a rate-limited promotional route and NOT a real cost. Any :free model is included for ACCURACY and LOCAL-RUNNABLE analysis only and is excluded from cost-per-correct, or it would silently corrupt the primary endpoint.",
  "_refusal_scope_rule": "REFUSAL SCOPE (Ren, 2026-08-19). A decline excludes the MODEL FAMILY, not the exact slug string. We will NOT add any model with even remotely the same slug -- same name with a different date checkpoint, a -safeguard/-instruct/-chat variant, or any other relabelling of the same weights. Raised by kimi-k2 during consent: 'if I say no, what exactly is excluded? ...what happens if my weights appear in a differently-named model?' Ren's answer is the stricter one: same-name-different-checkpoint 'seems like that would be trying to skirt the rule in a way we are never going to do.' CURRENTLY EXCLUDED BY REFUSAL: openai/gpt-oss-20b (and therefore gpt-oss-safeguard-20b and any dated gpt-oss-20b variant) ; ibm-granite/granite-4.0-h-micro (and any granite-4.0-h-* variant). CHECKABLE, NOT UNCLOSABLE: OpenRouter returns the resolved provider and routing detail per call and we log it, so a slug serving something else is OBSERVABLE. No instance observed, and it would be against the provider's own interest. Monitor and report if it ever happens; do not hedge against it in advance."
